#!/usr/bin/env bash
# verify-round —— open one round of the fully-real manual verification.
#
# A round gets its OWN directory, named by the time it started. Everything the round produces
# lives there: the run sheet it works down, and one self-contained trajectory folder per module
# (its md next to its own shots/). The directory is gitignored — it is evidence of a run, not a
# document about the product. Only two things ever leave it: a row in
# docs/real-env-verification/findings.md and a row in ux.md. (SOP iron rule 1: a clean pass
# produces no artifact.)
#
#   make verify-round            # opens e2e/manual-runs/<UTC timestamp>/
#
# The run sheet is GENERATED from docs/real-env-verification/items/*.md, never hand-copied:
# a module added to the audit shows up in the next round's sheet by itself. A hand-maintained
# copy is the exact thing that rots into "the list looks complete" while a module is missing.

set -euo pipefail

ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)"
ITEMS="$ROOT/docs/real-env-verification/items"
STAMP="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H%M)"
ROUND="$ROOT/e2e/manual-runs/$STAMP"

[ -d "$ITEMS" ] || { echo "no items dir at $ITEMS" >&2; exit 1; }
[ -e "$ROUND" ] && { echo "round $STAMP already open at $ROUND" >&2; exit 1; }

mkdir -p "$ROUND/trajectory"

modules=()
while IFS= read -r f; do
  modules+=("$(basename "$f" .md)")
done < <(find "$ITEMS" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.md' | sort)

# ---- run sheet: one row per module, this round's ledger ----
{
  cat <<EOF
# Run sheet — round $STAMP

Work DOWN this table. One row per module in \`docs/real-env-verification/items/\`
(${#modules[@]} modules, generated at open — do not hand-edit the list).

**Result — does it work** (the manual chain)
- \`⬜\` not run yet
- \`✅\` manual green → **STOP** on this module. No finding, no test, no code change.
- \`🔴\` mismatch → record a row in \`docs/real-env-verification/findings.md\` as \`F-<letter>-<n>\`, then **keep going**
- \`⛔\` blocked (missing credential / hardware) · \`🚫\` de-scoped this round

**Design — is it any good** (the designer pass over this module's trajectory, SOP §1c)
- \`⬜\` not reviewed yet
- \`🎨✅\` **uiux designer verified** — a designer read the chain + shots and passed it
- \`🎨🟠\` issues → \`ux.md\` rows (UX-n). Name them in the Findings column.
- \`➖\` no visual surface (protocol-only module)

The two are independent: a module can work perfectly and fail design, or look right and be
broken. The UX eye stays open the whole time as well — log to \`ux.md\` the moment you see
something, don't wait for the designer pass (SOP iron rule 6).

| # | Module | Result | Design | Findings / UX raised | Trajectory |
|---|--------|--------|--------|----------------------|------------|
EOF
  i=0
  for m in "${modules[@]}"; do
    i=$((i + 1))
    printf '| %d | %s | ⬜ | ⬜ | | [trajectory](trajectory/%s/%s.md) |\n' "$i" "$m" "$m" "$m"
  done
  cat <<'EOF'

## Round notes

- Stack: `make prod-up` (zero mocks) · app :38227 · backend :8100 · project `standmeet-prod`
- Creds: `~/.config/standmeet/verify-creds.env`
- Driver: headed Playwright MCP against the shipped GUI. **Never verify at the DB / API / log
  layer during the manual phase** — ground truth is the product's own surfaces.
EOF
} > "$ROUND/runsheet.md"

# ---- one self-contained trajectory folder per module: its md + its own shots/ ----
for m in "${modules[@]}"; do
  mkdir -p "$ROUND/trajectory/$m/shots"
  cat > "$ROUND/trajectory/$m/$m.md" <<EOF
# $m — trajectory · round $STAMP

Guidance: \`docs/real-env-verification/items/$m.md\` (steps, expected, ⚠️ LOOK).

**How to fill this in.** Write the chain as you walk it, in order, one block per operation:
what you clicked, the shot of what came back, what you expected, what you saw. Shoot the
surface the moment it opens, before touching anything, and shoot again after EVERY operation.
Shots live in \`shots/NN-<slug>.png\` next to this file — this folder holds the whole module.

Shoot FULL PAGE, not the viewport crop: the designer pass below reads these shots instead of
re-driving the GUI, and it cannot judge composition from a cropped screen.

## 00 — opened <where>

![opened](shots/00-open.png)

- Expected:
- Saw:
- First impression (task-free, SOP §1b):

## 01 — clicked <what>

![result](shots/01-.png)

- Expected:
- Saw:
- Verdict: ✅ / 🔴 F-?-? / 👀 UX-?

## 02 — typed <what> / went to <where>

![result](shots/02-.png)

- Expected:
- Saw:
- Verdict:

---

## 🎨 Design review (SOP §1c)

Run the \`critique\` skill (and \`audit\` for accessibility / theming / responsive) over the chain
and shots ABOVE. This section is why the trajectory exists: the designer judges the same
surfaces the functional pass drove, without re-driving them.

- Reviewed with: \`critique\` / \`audit\`
- **Verdict:** 🎨✅ uiux designer verified · 🎨🟠 issues below · ➖ no visual surface
- Issues raised (each also gets a \`ux.md\` row):
  - UX-?? · sev 🔴/🟠/🟡/💡 ·
- Held up well:
EOF
done

echo "round open: $ROUND"
echo "  run sheet:  $ROUND/runsheet.md  (${#modules[@]} modules)"
echo "  per module: $ROUND/trajectory/<module>/{<module>.md, shots/}"
